        "title": "Computational Fluid Dynamics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CFD is the numerical solution of the governing equations of fluid dynamics. It is the \"third pillar\" of fluid mechanics alongside theory and experiment. The field connects fluid physics to algorithm design: different equation types require different discretization strategies, and the nonlinearity of Navier-Stokes imposes unique stability constraints. From the MIT TCS background, CFD is applied numerical linear algebra + time-stepping algorithms + domain decomposition — running at petascale and beyond."
    }
